\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Profile likelihood of the klystron's (a) amplitude compression $g_A$ and (b) AM/PM conversion $k_\mathrm  {AP}$ at the \SI {497}{mA} operating point, with both free at every operating point, for nested data sets: the loop band of one record (\SIrange {25}{550}{kHz}), the same record over the full band, the gain and phase scan at \SI {497}{mA}, and all records. Every other parameter is re-optimized at each point; the dotted line marks the 95\% level ($\Delta \chi ^2=3.84$). The vertical axis is linear below 10.}}{6}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
