\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces The klystron in the trip records (present tube, 2021). (a) Ratio of the relative fluctuations of output and drive amplitude against frequency, for the records at full output (blue) and at the no-beam output (orange); shaded: \SIrange {50}{200}{kHz}. (b) AM/PM conversion from the probe's response to drive amplitude and phase, per record (band: mean $\pm $ standard deviation); crosses: the values of the closed-loop fit with $k_\mathrm  {AP}$ free at every operating point. (c) Compression identified from the closed-loop records at each operating point (squares) and as one value for all currents (dashed), against the trip records at \SIrange {50}{200}{kHz} (band) and above \SI {200}{kHz} (dotted); top axis: HVPS voltage estimated from the power balance at the fixed drive.}}{7}{figure.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:trips}{{3}{7}{The klystron in the trip records (present tube, 2021). (a) Ratio of the relative fluctuations of output and drive amplitude against frequency, for the records at full output (blue) and at the no-beam output (orange); shaded: \SIrange {50}{200}{kHz}. (b) AM/PM conversion from the probe's response to drive amplitude and phase, per record (band: mean $\pm $ standard deviation); crosses: the values of the closed-loop fit with $\kAP $ free at every operating point. (c) Compression identified from the closed-loop records at each operating point (squares) and as one value for all currents (dashed), against the trip records at \SIrange {50}{200}{kHz} (band) and above \SI {200}{kHz} (dotted); top axis: HVPS voltage estimated from the power balance at the fixed drive}{figure.3}{}}
